The code statements that lead to the bug are:
svm_copy_vmloadsave_state(svm->vmcb, vmcb12);
svm_copy_vmloadsave_state(vmcb12, svm->vmcb);
Reason:
When VMLOAD/VMSAVE is emulated for an L2 guest that is not intercepted, the code uses `svm->vmcb`, which points to the current VMCB (vmcb02 for L2). This incorrectly reads or writes the L2 VMCB fields instead of the L1 VMCB (vmcb01), causing guest state corruption.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
svm_copy_vmloadsave_state(svm->vmcb01.ptr, vmcb12);
svm_copy_vmloadsave_state(vmcb12, svm->vmcb01.ptr);
Reason:
The fix replaces `svm->vmcb` with `svm->vmcb01.ptr`, ensuring VMLOAD/VMSAVE always operates on the L1 VMCB (vmcb01), matching the hardware behavior where these instructions always affect the host (L1) state regardless of the current guest mode.

